< The news dataset is constructed from GDELT GKG 2.0, a large-scale global database designed to measure events, locations, and tone from news sources \citep{leetaru2013gdelt}. The extraction covers 46 months from 29 September 2022 to 21 June 2026 and uses four multilingual query groups related to Russian attacks, Ukrainian defense and energy, the defense industry, and the energy consequences of the war. The raw extraction produced approximately 12 million article-query observations, which were reduced to about 11.4 million URL-deduplicated observations.
---
> The classifier applies four tiers in order. Syndication platforms with no newsroom of their own are excluded first, because they carry large volume but no editorial voice. A curated register of the highest-volume outlets is applied next, recording country and, for Russian outlets, state control as against independent or exile ownership. Country top-level domains are applied third. Source language is applied last and only where country remains unknown. Country resolves before language because many Ukrainian outlets publish heavily in Russian, so a language-first rule would file them as Russian media and manufacture agreement between the two groups; Section~\ref{sec:classcheck} reports what such a rule costs in practice.
142c163
< News sources are classified into Ukrainian, Russian, Western, and other groups. The classifier combines manually curated source domains, country information extracted from GDELT location fields, top-level-domain heuristics, and a fallback category. This hybrid approach is useful because domain-only classification has high precision but low coverage, while country information provides much broader coverage. An automated agreement check on high-confidence domains reports overall agreement of approximately 85.4 percent, with higher agreement for manually classified domains and top-level-domain rules.
---
> Five source groups enter the tests: Ukrainian, Russian state, Russian independent, Western, and native-English. Russian outlets outside the register are retained as a residual group that is reported but not tested, so that unclassified Russian volume remains visible rather than hidden inside another series.
