< The daily news variables measure both attention and tone. Attention is the number of articles in a given source group and query category. Tone is the average GDELT tone score for articles in a given group and day. Because GDELT tone is a scalable automated measure, it is interpreted as an indicator of article negativity or positivity rather than a perfect measure of investor sentiment. This interpretation follows the broader caution in financial textual analysis that dictionaries and automated textual scores may behave differently across domains \citep{loughran2011textual}.
